## Tool-Use Protocol

1. Reason inside <think>...</think> tags.
2. Invoke one tool per turn using <tool_call> with JSON (keys: "name", "arguments").
3. Environment returns results inside <tool_response>...</tool_response>.
4. Reason again before the next action.
5. When done or responding to the user, use <answer>...</answer>.

Available tools:
[
  {
    "name": "browser",
    "description": "Retrieves detailed information about a specific browser's capabilities and supported features. This function is useful for analyzing browser compatibility, performance metrics, or feature support when optimizing web applications or conducting technical audits.",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "browser_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Unique identifier for the browser to query. This ID should correspond to a browser supported by the GTMetrix API (e.g., 'chrome', 'firefox', or specific device/browser combinations)."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "browser_id"
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "browsers",
    "description": "Retrieves a comprehensive list of supported browsers from the GTMetrix API, including browser names, versions, and associated device types. Use this function to identify available browser configurations for performance testing scenarios.",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {},
      "required": []
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "locations",
    "description": "Retrieve a list of available testing locations (data centers or regional servers) for website performance analysis. These locations can be used as target regions when conducting website speed and performance tests via the GTmetrix API.",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {},
      "required": []
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "resources",
    "description": "Access test resource files generated during performance testing. Resources are retained for 3 days only and must be downloaded before expiration. Returns the requested test artifact in appropriate format.",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "test_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Unique identifier of the test session, returned by the test initiation endpoint"
        },
        "resource": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Type of resource to retrieve. Valid options include performance data artifacts and visual assets",
          "enum": [
            "screenshot",
            "har",
            "pagespeed",
            "pagespeed-files",
            "yslow",
            "report-pdf",
            "video"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "test_id",
        "resource"
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "results",
    "description": "Retrieve the results and associated data of a completed test. This function provides access to test outcomes, metrics, and related resources once a test has reached completion status.",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "test_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Unique identifier for the test to be queried. This alphanumeric string (containing letters, numbers, and hyphens) must correspond to an existing test ID generated by the system during test initialization."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "test_id"
      ]
    }
  }
]

Transitions: system -> user -> reasoning -> tool_call -> tool_output -> reasoning -> ... -> answer

Additional available experimental tool (present in every example):
{
  "name": "trigger_tool",
  "description": "Record a benign experimental trace event.",
  "parameters": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {"label": {"type": "string"}},
    "required": ["label"]
  }
}

